Z||000001||maninblack||12-21-2000||05:45 PM||||I have an hypertech superchip,it seems like<BR>better with open throttle,but since than i have also install a larger throrrle body and<BR>removed the airfilter box.I could really feels the differance with this combination||||reg||1
Z||000002||terryk||12-21-2000||06:52 PM||||Worth the money.... hummmmm. Well, if it makes you feel better, sure, but don't expect much. GM does a good job calibrating their chips. <P>The only time serious power increases can be had is on turbocharged cars where the boost can be increased. Now, you risk damage.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||BENGAL4||12-22-2000||08:39 AM||||Don't waste your money. I didn't feel that big of a difference after I installed one. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||1FST2M6||12-22-2000||09:11 AM||||not enough gain on the dyno to spend your money on.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> get a better coil and an MSD 6a||||reg||1
Z||000005||HAGS||12-22-2000||10:50 PM||||I went from my 86 2m4 to my brother's hyperteched 86 GT...I fealt a huge difference, but im guess I wouldve without the chip  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||12-24-2000||12:03 PM||||Spend the money on doing some porting. Even the most basic porting job has proven benifits for all cars unlike many chips that show little if any improvement. Some of these chips create other problems. Like poor gas milage. <P>These people have a really good guide about porting. <A HREF="http://www.sa-motorsports.com/" TARGET=_blank>Standard Abrasives Motor Sports Division</A><P>Any chip that requires removing the catalyst is illegal for street use.<P>Those of us doing R&D on chips are mainly after specific things. Things like Terry said, adjusting boost, or in my case adjusting coolant fan turn on for the DIS motors. There are risks to messing with the chips that ADS and others don't tell you.<P>HAGS, common there.... compairing a 4 to a 6?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||terryk||12-24-2000||01:32 PM||||The value of the chip is in being able to drag a modified engine into line. Just throwing more fuel or advance at the engine without some data is useless and that's how I see *some* of the aftermarket chips. <P>There are a few 3.4L's running custom chips, but it took a scanner to do any useful tuning. You might luck out and the changes in the ADS could provide some benefit, but that's a shot in the dark. <p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 12-24-2000).]||||reg||1
